# Installation

Loom is one command-line program, `loom`. You install it once, and it works in every project on your computer. It runs on Bun, or on Node.js 22 or later.

## Install the command

Choose the package manager you already use. The command changes with your choice, and the button copies it for you.

```install
```

## Check that it works

Ask Loom for its version:

```bash
loom --version
```

It prints the version you installed. Run `loom` on its own, with nothing after it, to see every command it knows.

## Update later

To move to a newer release, run the same install command again. It always fetches the latest version.

## Anything else to install?

No. Loom writes TypeScript out of the box. Support for another language comes as a package you add to a project when you need it, not as a new version of Loom.
